8. DIGITAL ASSETS AND YOUR RESPONSIBILITIES

8.1 You are solely responsible for:

    (a) your wallet, seed phrase, passphrase, private keys, WIF, API keys, node, device, and network security;

    (b) every transaction, transfer, swap, escrow arrangement, marketplace trade, fee, and counterparty you choose;

    (c) verifying every address, name, amount, fee, script, and chain state before signing or broadcasting anything;

    (d) maintaining independent backups; and

    (e) your tax, legal, accounting, and regulatory compliance.

8.2 Blockchain transactions are generally irreversible. Digital assets are volatile and can be lost, stolen, frozen, or rendered worthless. Network fees are non-refundable. We cannot reverse a transaction, recover a lost seed phrase or passphrase, restore a lost key, or retrieve funds sent to the wrong address.

8.3 We do not provide custody, exchange, brokerage, investment, legal, tax, or accounting services. We are not a party to any marketplace, escrow, or swap transaction. We do not guarantee that a counterparty will deliver a name, pay a price, complete a swap, or act honestly. We do not guarantee liquidity, arbitration, dispute resolution, or recovery of funds.

8.4 The Software is not financial, investment, legal, or tax advice. You are responsible for your own decisions. Use small amounts and test on testnet or regtest where possible.

9. EXPERIMENTAL FEATURES

9.1 Marketplace, escrow, atomic swap, DGB, and Nostr features are experimental. They may not have completed a funded end-to-end trade on both chains. They may fail, lose funds, or behave unexpectedly.

9.2 Escrow uses an external arbiter that you choose. We do not provide, control, endorse, or supervise arbiters. An arbiter may collude with a counterparty, make mistakes, or become unavailable. Lost keys can deadlock escrowed funds. There may be no timeout refund.

9.3 You are responsible for choosing counterparties, arbiters, relays, Electrum servers, nodes, and networks. Use independent verification and start with small amounts.

10. PRIVACY AND DATA

10.1 The Software is local-first. As of this version, it does not require a Handess account and does not send data to a Handess-operated backend. It stores settings and wallet-related data on your device.

10.2 The Software connects directly to the node, Electrum-DGB server, Nostr relays, and price data provider that you configure. Those third parties may see your IP address, public keys, names, amounts, and other metadata. Marketplace and swap coordination events are public by design. Purchase-intent payloads may be encrypted, but metadata can still leak.

10.3 You are responsible for what you publish to public networks and for protecting your device and local data. This version does not include analytics or advertising SDKs.

